# Central config. Source this; don't hardcode these values anywhere else.
JARVIS_AGENCY=actuator          # advisory | actuator | agentic
# Camera. 0 = /dev/video0 (built-in webcam).
# Phone as camera: install "IP Webcam" (Android), start the server, and put
# its URL here — e.g. http://192.168.1.42:8080/video
# Lock focus and exposure in the app; autofocus hunting wrecks hand tracking.
JARVIS_CAM=0
# Fast resident model: banter, wake responses, tool routing. Answers most
# turns entirely on its own — a 7B benchmarks at 100% tool accuracy here.
JARVIS_CHAT_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b

# Handed the hard problems, via the reason.deeply tool. The FAST model decides
# when to escalate, so this only runs when a question actually warrants it.
# Leave empty to disable escalation entirely.
#
# What fits on this machine — 24 GB VRAM (7900 XTX) + 64 GB RAM, so about
# 80 GB usable once the desktop has its share. Sizes are Ollama's own, checked
# 2026-10-24, not estimated:
#
#   qwen3.8:27b                18 GB   resident in VRAM, room for context.
#                                      Newest generation; vision + tools.
#   qwen3.5:35b-a3b            22 GB   MoE, 3B active. Tight in VRAM and fast
#                                      because only 3B is computed per token.
#   qwen3.5:27b                17 GB   the safe dense choice.
#   qwen3.5:122b-a10b          81 GB   MoE, 10B active. Right ON the line:
#                                      it loads with nothing spare, so KV
#                                      cache pushes it to paging from disk.
#                                      Possible, not comfortable.
#   qwen3.8-flash-next        105 GB   smallest published quant (q4_K_M is
#                                      120 GB). 125B total, 6B active, but a
#                                      51B n-gram embedding table is counted
#                                      in — which is what makes it not fit.
#                                      25 GB over even the optimistic pool.
#
# MoE is the thing to look for here, not parameter count: 35b-a3b computes 3B
# per token, so it answers like a small model while knowing like a large one.
# For JARVIS's two model jobs — describing a mechanism in a closed trait
# vocabulary, and binding a genome under a grammar — a bigger model is not
# obviously better, and `jarvis figure-bench <models...>` is there to settle
# it rather than argue about it.
JARVIS_HEAVY_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b
# Reasoning models (Hermes 4, Qwen 3.x) work unmodified — <think> blocks are
# stripped before speech and text-form <tool_call> tags are executed anyway.
# See core/reasoning.py.
JARVIS_VOICE=en_GB-alan-medium  # Piper voice (dry British male)

# The Atlas physics tier — thermal, structural, the checker battery, the
# independent cross-check. Runs out of process (scripts/atlas_worker.py)
# because both projects own a package called `core` and there is no import
# order that satisfies both. Leave it pointing at nothing and the design
# tools that need it are simply not registered.
JARVIS_ATLAS_ROOT=~/atlas-research

# The anatomy skill ships in the repo at .claude/skills/anatomy, so `/anatomy`
# is available to Claude Code in this project and `node build.mjs` in a figure
# directory needs nothing installed. Set ANATOMY_ROOT only to build a figure
# against a different checkout.
